[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2697810078","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103506#issuecomment-2697810078","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103506","id":2697810078,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gzVCe","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-04T14:22:16Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T14:22:16Z","body":"I'm a fan of the concept of named pools, but does this implementation mean that it'll double up the available thread count from whatever the user configured? I've looked at the PR and didn't see if we have any logic to handle on how to respect that setting.\r\n\r\nIt's still an acceptable hotfix in my eyes as the workload for shader compilation doesn't come in that frequently.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2697810078/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2697835627","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103506#issuecomment-2697835627","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103506","id":2697835627,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gzbRr","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-04T14:30:44Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T14:30:44Z","body":"> I'm a fan of the concept of named pools, but does this implementation mean that it'll double up the available thread count from whatever the user configured?\r\n\r\nYes, it is doubling the number of threads (we do not want to constantly spawn new threads, but simply having 2 threads per core should not cuase any problems).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2697835627/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2698341812","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103506#issuecomment-2698341812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103506","id":2698341812,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6g1W20","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-04T16:59:58Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T16:59:58Z","body":"I am a little bit unclear about the tradeoffs here. We are spawning a bunch of extra threads that will ultimately sit idle. Will they consume any resources once we finish compiling shaders? Are their any OS limitations we need to be wary of (especially on Mobile/Web)?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2698341812/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2698376115","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103506#issuecomment-2698376115","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103506","id":2698376115,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6g1fOz","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-04T17:12:57Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T17:29:54Z","body":"> Web\r\n\r\nWe do not have WebGPU support (RenderingDevice), so it will have zero effect on web.\r\n\r\n> Are their any OS limitations we need to be wary of\r\n\r\nThere is a per-process handle limit, but as far as I know it's in the thousands or tens of thousands depending on platform.\r\n\r\n> Will they consume any resources once we finish compiling shaders?\r\n\r\n512 KiB of memory for stack + metadata per thread. At least on macOS, Xcode profiler show completely flat line for idle threads with no detectable CPU activity at all.\r\n\r\nAlso, the new pool is only initialized if there are shaders to compile, as long as it's loaded from cache it won't, so it should affect only the first start or editor.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2698376115/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2701356549","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103506#issuecomment-2701356549","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103506","id":2701356549,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hA24F","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-05T15:52:35Z","updated_at":"2025-03-05T15:52:35Z","body":"> I am concerned that this named WTP system will get blindly expanded in the future into some sort of generic feature, but I think for now we should go forward with this PR\r\n\r\nThat's the main reason I do not want to create a nice API for it, and implemented it as a single function. It won't prevent it from being used, but at least have more chances for a comment advising not to use it to be noticed.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2701356549/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":nul